        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis seems to be have the same culprit as #653, i.e. it is an upstream nvim-neo-tree/neo-tree.nvim#1211 issue with 'neo-tree.nvim' blocking events which 'mini.statusline' uses to detect when active/inactive content should be set. And using that type of events (`WinEnter` in particular) is indeed the best approach to do that.\r\n\r\nClosing as not an issue with 'mini.statusline'.",
